cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article below."
title: "TAME: Triangular AlignMEnt"
abstract: >-
  TAME globally aligns two networks by maximising the number of conserved
  triangles. The objective is relaxed to a third-order tensor Z-eigenvector
  problem, solved with a shifted symmetric higher-order power method, and
  rounded to a one-to-one mapping by b-matching.
type: software
